    {
      "additions": 1,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/c59a82821e5c1e883fc374a1f9116f2a610684a5/docs%2Fuser-guide%2Fdata-loading.md",
      "changes": 2,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/contents/docs%2Fuser-guide%2Fdata-loading.md?ref=c59a82821e5c1e883fc374a1f9116f2a610684a5",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "docs/user-guide/data-loading.md",
      "patch": "@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@ torchrun --nproc_per_node=8 --nnodes=512 ... pretrain_gpt.py \\\n | `--per-dataset-sequences-path` | None | **Set when blending many datasets** | Points to a JSON file mapping each dataset path to its `(sequence_count, document_count)`. Replaces per-file metadata reads with a single JSON lookup. Generate with `tools/build_sequences_per_dataset.py`. |\n | `--data-cache-path` | None | **Set** | Directory where index `.npy` files are cached. Must be on shared storage for multi-node jobs so all ranks can read it. |\n | `--num-workers` | 2 | **Keep as small as necessary** | Number of DataLoader worker processes. The goal is to satisfy: *time to process a batch > time to prepare a batch*. This hides dataloader work behind the training step. Increasing beyond what's needed wastes CPU and memory. |\n-| `--no-mmap-bin-files` | mmap on | **Test both** | Memory-mapping `.bin` files leverages the OS page cache, but the optimal setting is filesystem-dependent. Some large-scale production configurations disable mmap. Test with and without to determine what works best for your storage. |\n+| `--no-mmap-bin-files` | mmap on | **Test both** | Memory-mapping `.bin` files leverages the OS page cache, but the optimal setting is filesystem-dependent. For large blends that fail with mmap-related `PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not permitted` (EPERM), try this flag: it removes the `.bin` mapping per dataset while `.idx` remains mapped. See the [reported WekaFS case](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/issues/3968). Test with and without to determine what works best for your storage. |\n \n ### Object storage (S3 / Multi-Storage Client)\n ",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/raw/c59a82821e5c1e883fc374a1f9116f2a610684a5/docs%2Fuser-guide%2Fdata-loading.md",
      "sha": "04de9f25ae54f3c153e908295a4b23a72944bd47",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 10,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/c59a82821e5c1e883fc374a1f9116f2a610684a5/megatron%2Fcore%2Fdatasets%2Fblended_megatron_dataset_config.py",
      "changes": 11,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/contents/megatron%2Fcore%2Fdatasets%2Fblended_megatron_dataset_config.py?ref=c59a82821e5c1e883fc374a1f9116f2a610684a5",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "megatron/core/datasets/blended_megatron_dataset_config.py",
      "patch": "@@ -58,7 +58,16 @@ class BlendedMegatronDatasetConfig:\n     \"\"\"Where all re-useable dataset indices are to be cached.\"\"\"\n \n     mmap_bin_files: bool = True\n-    \"\"\"Whether to mmap the .bin files or use file pointers.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Whether to mmap the .bin files or use file pointers.\n+\n+       Set to False for object storage backends (e.g. S3), where mmap is not supported.\n+       It can also mitigate mmap-related ``PermissionError: [Errno 1] Operation not\n+       permitted`` (EPERM) during construction of large dataset blends. A WekaFS report\n+       in NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge#3968 suspected a filesystem-client mmap limit;\n+       that cause was not established. File-pointer reads remove the ``.bin`` mapping\n+       per dataset; ``.idx`` remains mapped. Measure the throughput impact on your storage.\n+       See ``--no-mmap-bin-files`` in docs/user-guide/data-loading.md.\n+    \"\"\"\n \n     mock: bool = field(init=False, default=False)\n     \"\"\"Whether to bypass real data loading and validation in favor of mock data generation.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/raw/c59a82821e5c1e883fc374a1f9116f2a610684a5/megatron%2Fcore%2Fdatasets%2Fblended_megatron_dataset_config.py",
      "sha": "460d3befe4580c1e16dbef0adf181da891faa1a3",
      "status": "modified"
    }
